  "ledger_new_four_literal_cells": [
    "30005455 / OWR-12697708-008: Sharp Reinforcement Thresholds for Tree and Whisker Components",
    "",
    "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23592692",
    "A sharp forest bound and an improved whisker bound for finite WARM graphs — Alec Kriebel (ORCID 0009-0001-9320-500X), v1.0.0 (2026-10-21). Unrefereed preprint. For finite simple undirected loopless graphs, arbitrary positive vertex firing rates and arbitrary fixed positive integer initial edge counts, surviving support is almost surely a forest for alpha > 4/3. The known equal-rate unit triangle supplies the strict lower obstruction. For equal positive rates every surviving component has diameter at most three for alpha >= 17/4. Both literal OWR12/2023 printed655 numerical-improvement requests (forest bound2 and equal-rate whisker bound25) are answered. The suggested sharp whisker interval 4/3 < alpha < 17/4 and stochastic endpoint alpha = 4/3 remain unresolved. No arbitrary positive real initialization, infinite-graph, loop or multigraph theorem. Published HHK2023 convergence/support inputs, even-cycle/uniform odd-cycle methods, triangle obstruction and HK2017 least-weight/champion mechanism are credited; the earlier proof already implies a weaker whisker bound at24. Two bounded independent primary-source priority investigations recovered no earlier full universal bound; no exhaustive priority, worldwide firstness, first public availability or current global-openness certificate. PDF and editable-source/verification ZIP preserve all eight original submissions, distinct mathematical/priority audits and exact finite controls. Computation supplements the universal proof. Extensive AI involvement in research, proof development, computation, adversarial auditing, literature investigation and writing. No formal independent human peer review, journal acceptance or proof-assistant certification. Source: DOI 10.4171/owr/2023/12, printed655. Record: https://zenodo.org/records/23592692. PR: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1131."
  ],
